    "gold_why": {
      "type": "section",
      "blocks": {
        "text_04": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>Why gold?</h2>",
            "width": "fit-content",
            "max_width": "none",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "custom",
            "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "font_size": "3.5rem",
            "weight": "300",
            "line_height": "tight",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "background": false,
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 28,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0,
            "font_size_mobile": "2.5rem"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "numbered_step_01": {
          "type": "numbered-step",
          "settings": {
            "number": "01",
            "title": "Inflation protection",
            "text": "Governments can create money without limit, and when debts grow, quietly eroding the currency is often the easiest way out. Gold follows a different logic: it is a finite resource, and extracting it is slow, costly and difficult to accelerate. That natural scarcity means your savings are measured in something that cannot be diluted at will.",
            "show_line": true,
            "number_column": 128,
            "gap": 6,
            "number_color": "#c4a35a",
            "title_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "body_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color1 }}",
            "body_opacity": 85,
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 40,
            "number_preset": "custom",
            "number_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "number_font_size": "2rem",
            "title_preset": "custom",
            "title_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "title_font_size": "1.75rem",
            "title_weight": "300",
            "body_preset": "custom",
            "body_font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "body_font_size": "0.875rem",
            "text_beside": true,
            "text_share": 50,
            "line_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
            "number_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem",
            "title_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "numbered_step_02": {
          "type": "numbered-step",
          "settings": {
            "number": "02",
            "title": "Crisis resilience",
            "text": "Most assets rise and fall together because they depend on the same economy. Gold moves to its own rhythm, and it tends to strengthen when fear takes hold. That makes it the rare asset that works hardest exactly when the rest of your portfolio needs support.",
            "show_line": true,
            "number_column": 128,
            "gap": 6,
            "number_color": "#c4a35a",
            "title_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "body_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color1 }}",
            "body_opacity": 85,
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 40,
            "number_preset": "custom",
            "number_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "number_font_size": "2rem",
            "title_preset": "custom",
            "title_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "title_font_size": "1.75rem",
            "title_weight": "300",
            "body_preset": "custom",
            "body_font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "body_font_size": "0.875rem",
            "text_beside": true,
            "text_share": 50,
            "line_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
            "number_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem",
            "title_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "numbered_step_03": {
          "type": "numbered-step",
          "settings": {
            "number": "03",
            "title": "Independence",
            "text": "Nearly every financial asset is someone else's promise: a bank's, a company's or a government's. When that promise breaks, the asset breaks with it. Gold is no one's liability, so its value rests on the metal itself and not on anyone keeping their word.",
            "show_line": true,
            "number_column": 128,
            "gap": 6,
            "number_color": "#c4a35a",
            "title_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "body_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color1 }}",
            "body_opacity": 85,
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 40,
            "number_preset": "custom",
            "number_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "number_font_size": "2rem",
            "title_preset": "custom",
            "title_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "title_font_size": "1.75rem",
            "title_weight": "300",
            "body_preset": "custom",
            "body_font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "body_font_size": "0.875rem",
            "text_beside": true,
            "text_share": 50,
            "line_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
            "number_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem",
            "title_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "numbered_step_04": {
          "type": "numbered-step",
          "settings": {
            "number": "04",
            "title": "Institutional conviction",
            "text": "Central banks, the very institutions that issue the world's currencies, are among gold's most committed buyers. They hold it because they understand better than anyone the limits of the currencies they issue. Following their lead means aligning with the most informed players in the global economy.",
            "show_line": true,
            "number_column": 128,
            "gap": 6,
            "number_color": "#c4a35a",
            "title_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "body_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color1 }}",
            "body_opacity": 85,
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 40,
            "number_preset": "custom",
            "number_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "number_font_size": "2rem",
            "title_preset": "custom",
            "title_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "title_font_size": "1.75rem",
            "title_weight": "300",
            "body_preset": "custom",
            "body_font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "body_font_size": "0.875rem",
            "text_beside": true,
            "text_share": 50,
            "line_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
            "number_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem",
            "title_font_size_mobile": "1.5rem"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "numbered_step_05": {
          "type": "numbered-step",
          "settings": {
            "number": "05",
            "title": "Global liquidity",
            "text": "Gold is universally recognized and valued, regardless of language, border or political system. That universality means it can always be converted into cash, anywhere in the world. Few assets offer protection and flexibility at the same time.",
            "show_line": true,
            "number_column": 128,
            "gap": 6,
            "number_color": "#c4a35a",
            "title_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.background }}",
            "body_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color1 }}",
            "body_opacity": 85,
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 40,
            "number_preset": "custom",
            "number_font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "number_font_size": "2rem",
